{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40270596",
      "title": "Using Keys For Resetting Components",
      "sourceHash": "60295f5d7fc14dd057b218466050ec187b5634589e9abb41c08f209c626e7182",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 2.07,
          "en": "So as you can tell by now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 6.03,
          "en": "keys are important in lists like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.03,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "But as I'll show you now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 11.43,
          "en": "keys are actually not just useful in lists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.43,
          "end": 14.34,
          "en": "Instead, let's go back to the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 17.01,
          "en": "Here, we're managing this chosen count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.01,
          "end": 20.583,
          "en": "which we're passing as an initial count value to counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.96,
          "end": 25.98,
          "en": "But at the moment, if I change this value and click set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.98,
          "end": 28.44,
          "en": "not a lot changes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.44,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "I mean, if you watch closely,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.91,
          "end": 31.811,
          "en": "you saw that this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.811,
          "end": 36.39,
          "en": "and this value here changed or was affected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.39,
          "end": 38.73,
          "en": "For example, if I enter a prime number here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.73,
          "end": 43.73,
          "en": "this also changed, but this value does not change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 46.47,
          "en": "And indeed, my idea here is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.47,
          "end": 48.69,
          "en": "as we enter a new value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.69,
          "end": 51.39,
          "en": "we then also reset this counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.39,
          "end": 53.193,
          "en": "to the value we entered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.6,
          "end": 56.01,
          "en": "But that's not happening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.01,
          "end": 58.74,
          "en": "because this initial count value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "is really just used as an initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 65.463,
          "en": "for the state when it's being initialized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.48,
          "end": 70.35,
          "en": "This initial value you pass to useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.35,
          "end": 73.62,
          "en": "is never used after the first execution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.62,
          "end": 75.72,
          "en": "of this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.72,
          "end": 79.95,
          "en": "It's really just used for initialization, nothing else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.95,
          "end": 83.943,
          "en": "And that's why future initial account changes are ignored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.23,
          "end": 88.02,
          "en": "But what if you now want to reset the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.02,
          "end": 90.18,
          "en": "if this prop changes?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.18,
          "end": 95.18,
          "en": "Well, one thing you could do is you could use useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 100.293,
          "en": "Here, we could import useEffect in this file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 104.67,
          "en": "And then in the counter component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.67,
          "end": 106.22999999999999,
          "en": "for example, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.22999999999999,
          "end": 111.22999999999999,
          "en": "we can execute useEffect, pass our effect function to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.47999999999999,
          "end": 113.343,
          "en": "and the dependencies array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.18,
          "end": 118.57,
          "en": "And then here we could add initial count as a dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.55,
          "end": 120.91,
          "en": "and call setCounterChanges",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.51,
          "end": 128.51,
          "en": "and basically set this to a new, almost, empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.64,
          "end": 132.18,
          "en": "where we just have this one initial value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.18,
          "end": 134.253,
          "en": "which is based on the initial count.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.39,
          "end": 138.933,
          "en": "And with that, we would basically reset this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 143.76,
          "en": "So now if I save that and I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.76,
          "end": 146.76,
          "en": "I can edit this counter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.76,
          "end": 149.79,
          "en": "But if I now enter a new value here and click set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.79,
          "end": 152.103,
          "en": "you see this is reset, this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.32999999999998,
          "end": 156.15,
          "en": "Now this approach would work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.15,
          "end": 158.43,
          "en": "but you're actually encouraged",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.43,
          "end": 161.67000000000002,
          "en": "to limit the usage of useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.67000000000002,
          "end": 165.63,
          "en": "because it is often used in a suboptimal way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 170.61,
          "en": "and it also triggers an extra component execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.61,
          "end": 173.76,
          "en": "Because, after all, you learned that this function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.76,
          "end": 177.81,
          "en": "runs after the component function execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.81,
          "end": 180.21,
          "en": "And if you then change the state in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.21,
          "end": 182.64,
          "en": "you, of course, trigger another",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.64,
          "end": 184.74,
          "en": "component function execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.74,
          "end": 187.59,
          "en": "So you have two component function executions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.59,
          "end": 188.82,
          "en": "instead of one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.82,
          "end": 190.893,
          "en": "And that's not optimal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.79,
          "end": 193.62,
          "en": "Therefore, a better way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.62,
          "end": 197.07,
          "en": "of forcing a component functional reset,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.07,
          "end": 200.07,
          "en": "which in the end is what we want to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.07,
          "end": 202.07999999999998,
          "en": "when initial count changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.07999999999998,
          "end": 206.07,
          "en": "is to use a key on the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.07,
          "end": 208.14,
          "en": "So here on this counter component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 211.893,
          "en": "which uses this chosen count as an initial count value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.94,
          "end": 214.8,
          "en": "You can add a key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.8,
          "end": 218.79,
          "en": "because you can add the key prop to any component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.79,
          "end": 222.84,
          "en": "not just to Components that are used in a list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.84,
          "end": 227.84,
          "en": "And then here you could use the chosen count as a key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.6,
          "end": 231.24,
          "en": "If you're only doing that on one component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.24,
          "end": 232.82999999999998,
          "en": "if you would add it on two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 232.82999999999998,
          "end": 235.14,
          "en": "you would get a complaint by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 235.14,
          "end": 237.543,
          "en": "and you would have to find some other key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.41,
          "end": 240.69,
          "en": "But the nice thing now is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.69,
          "end": 243.63,
          "en": "that whenever the key value changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.63,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "so the chosen count state value changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.15,
          "end": 248.97,
          "en": "React will basically, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.97,
          "end": 252.24,
          "en": "throw away the old component instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.24,
          "end": 255.42,
          "en": "It will destroy it and recreate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.42,
          "end": 258.51,
          "en": "So as if it would be rendering this counter component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.51,
          "end": 260.4,
          "en": "for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.4,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "And therefore this is a nice trick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 265.05,
          "en": "or pattern, to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 265.05,
          "end": 269.16,
          "en": "which you should use if you have some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.16,
          "end": 271.47,
          "en": "that may change in apparent component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 271.47,
          "end": 272.85,
          "en": "as it's the case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.85,
          "end": 276.12,
          "en": "that should then lead to some child component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.12,
          "end": 279.39300000000003,
          "en": "like this counter component here, being reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.47,
          "end": 285.47,
          "en": "Because by using this approach and not using useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.69,
          "end": 288.96,
          "en": "and therefore we can also remove the import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.96,
          "end": 290.37,
          "en": "By using this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 290.37,
          "end": 294.36,
          "en": "we avoid this extra component function execution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 294.36,
          "end": 297.33,
          "en": "because now the old component is simply removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.33,
          "end": 299.46,
          "en": "and a new component of the same type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.46,
          "end": 301.59,
          "en": "is reinsert, that you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.59,
          "end": 303.45,
          "en": "and it's then executed by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.45,
          "end": 305.883,
          "en": "and it's therefore only executed once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.9,
          "end": 311.73,
          "en": "So if you save that all and you set a new state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.73,
          "end": 313.74,
          "en": "you see this works as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.74,
          "end": 316.263,
          "en": "but now in a slightly more efficient way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.19,
          "end": 320.523,
          "en": "So this is another nice pattern you should keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}